251
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:58,597
Alright, what's our plan of attack?

252
00:13:58,680 --> 00:14:02,297
The dog mountain stratum and the
everlasting stratum are all that remain.

253
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:05,337
I assume we'll want to bolster
our forces before we go!

254
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:09,097
Yeesh, kiko yu's shoes are
going to be really hard to fill?

255
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:13,517
Indeed, it's pivotal, and I'm afraid I
can't spare anyone else for this task.

256
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:17,717
As expected, I'm thinking I'll invite
someone from the Menagerie of Fools.

257
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:18,737
Have you lost it?

258
00:14:18,820 --> 00:14:21,437
The fool I have in mind
is talented and has

259
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:24,579
certain abilities that our
lineup is sorely lacking,

260
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,000
personality aside.

261
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:29,080
Yeah, can't argue on the talent front.

262
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:31,880
It's def-legit, despite that temperament.

263
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:33,957
Should we be concerned
that they both think

264
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:36,157
our next edition kind
of sucks as a person?

265
00:14:36,240 --> 00:14:38,500
We need all the help we can get.

266
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:40,317
Any idea where we can find him?

267
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:42,617
Though I can't say for
sure, I have a hunch.

268
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:45,940
And it will require travel
to a new stratum. Gotcha.

269
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:49,157
So we're going to the Dog
Mountain Stratum to find a fool.

270
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:52,299
A transfer circle should
more than get the job done.

271
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:57,220
Two days later, our group arrived
at the Dog Mountain Stratum.

272
00:14:57,500 --> 00:15:02,140
The name probably gave it away, but this
stratum has a giant dog-shaped rock.

273
00:15:02,820 --> 00:15:06,157
Decay rock aside, it's a marine
stratum with tiny islands.

274
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:09,577
I hope we can spare some time for
a little fishing while we're here.

275
00:15:09,660 --> 00:15:12,131
Captain Carry Oil does love to cast a rod.

276
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:16,117
I'd love to start doling out some
Hawaiian shirts and get the party started.

277
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:17,729
But we're not on vacation.

278
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:20,400
Oh, hey! Nice to meet you!

279
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,317
Fresh from a transfer circle?

280
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,997
Yep, we're here from the
Clear Flow Lake Stratum.

281
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:26,580
You are? That's great!

282
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:29,977
I've got to go tell the
director, so don't move an inch.

283
00:15:30,060 --> 00:15:32,417
Are you folks really from another stratum?

284
00:15:32,500 --> 00:15:33,540
You bet, mister.

285
00:15:34,060 --> 00:15:36,657
Thank goodness the transfer
circles are finally working.

286
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:39,737
Now we can eat something other
than seafood for a change.

287
00:15:39,820 --> 00:15:42,467
Did the monsters cause
any extra damage here?

288
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:46,337
Nah, we were plagued with frequent
monster attacks for a while there.

289
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:49,137
But then some incredible
hunters arrived and saved us.

290
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:52,817
Fortunately, that happened right before
the transfer circles stopped functioning.

291
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:54,194
So we made it through.

292
00:15:54,820 --> 00:15:56,480
If you don't mind me asking,

293
00:15:56,620 --> 00:15:59,337
did those hunters call themselves
the Menagerie of Fools?

294
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:01,080
Oh, so you know them.

295
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,150
Small world, eh?

296
00:16:02,233 --> 00:16:07,140
Well, that's not good, but it's
probably okay, right? It's fine.

297
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:09,660
In fact, they contacted us earlier.

298
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:10,977
But regardless,

299
00:16:11,060 --> 00:16:15,119
I highly doubt the director and the
others were able to convince her.

300
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,257
Hello, hello!

301
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:17,516
Thanks for visiting!

302
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,917
Make yourselves at home!

303
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,557
That looks like a kid, but I
guess it's the Stratum's director?

304
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:23,700
Oh, hello there!

305
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:24,697
It's been a while.

306
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:26,257
Yes, it most certainly has.

307
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:29,377
I'm the director of the Dog Mountain
Stratum's Hunters Association.

308
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:32,297
I brought you a letter
from Director Bear if you'd

309
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:35,262
like to take a look is
that a fact let me see oh.

310
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:40,497
This explains why the monsters
got so aggressive that's good

311
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:43,757
to know well good luck taking
care of all that weirdness.

312
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:46,428
You can let me know
when the job's finished?

313
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:48,422
Where do you think you're going?

314
00:16:50,060 --> 00:16:52,360
Sorry, please forgive his rudeness.

315
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:56,057
He's basically the babysitter
if I'm understanding

316
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:59,037
the situation You need us
to help you find someone?

317
00:16:59,120 --> 00:17:00,817
That's no problem whatsoever.

318
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:02,097
Can you describe them?

319
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:03,740
We greatly appreciate it.

320
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:06,391
I'll give you all the information we have.

321
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:13,700
While Heavy gave them the rundown, we
got to enjoy some primo relaxation.

322
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:16,380
How should we pass the time, Boxo?

323
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,640
I can't exactly go swimming.

324
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:22,317
The next best thing for a beach
day is to enjoy some fishing.

325
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:24,437
Tss, eef ood. Hmm?

326
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:28,200
Even my perceptive llamas
couldn't decipher that one.

327
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:30,700
It's tough not being able to talk.

328
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:32,360
I'll try again.

329
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,660
Cast-tat-la-tin. Hmm.

330
00:17:35,180 --> 00:17:36,060
Si-i-foo-n.

331
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,620
Cast-tat-la-in?

332
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,597
You're saying you want to go fishing.

333
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:40,540
Yes, yes.

334
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:42,747
Llamas is out of this world.

335
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:44,997
I wasn't sure that was going to work.

336
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:46,080
I did it.

337
00:17:46,180 --> 00:17:47,617
I knew I could figure it out.

338
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:50,229
All that's left is to
work out the details.

339
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:51,490
Yeah!

340
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:54,097
I really only know how
to do punchy fishing.

341
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:59,837
in a river that's technically not fishing
i love punchy fishing you can count me in!

342
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:02,017
but instead of using our
fists or nailing them

343
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:04,157
with rocks why don't we
try the laid back method?

344
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:06,257
for a change sounds fun!

345
00:18:06,340 --> 00:18:08,157
great now we just need
the right equipment.

346
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:13,457
look no further ladies your friendly
neighborhood voxos got you covered.

347
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:20,417
doesn't look like you
have any rods for sale?

348
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:23,320
But we can probably
just use a stick. I see.

349
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:27,197
Some bags have pictures of fishing
lines with floats and hooks attached.

350
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:29,339
But some only have symbols on them.

351
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:30,417
Are those baits?

352
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:31,330
Hello there.

353
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:33,837
I'll go find some nice sticks for us.

354
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:34,750
Great.

355
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,158
Almost time for the moment of truth.

356
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:39,617
A lot of girls scream
and cry and yell, Ew,

357
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:42,737
that's grody, when they see
bait for the first time.

358
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:46,055
I'm weirdly fascinated to
see how those two will react.

359
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:48,612
Their cute expressions will be priceless.

360
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:49,737
I'm going to record it.

361
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:50,650
for science.

362
00:18:51,220 --> 00:18:54,937
I've seen things like that, but a
little different at the river before.

363
00:18:55,020 --> 00:18:58,457
This is kid stuff compared to some
of the monsters I've come across.

364
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:00,069
Yeah, I guess that tracks.

365
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:02,737
Why did I expect them to
freak out over a little

366
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:05,761
worm when they fight ugly
monsters on the regular?

367
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:08,237
Let's make this a tad more interesting.

368
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:11,317
Whoever catches the biggest one
will be named the fishing champ.

369
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,837
I'm not going to hold back!

370
00:19:12,920 --> 00:19:13,750
Hello there.

371
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:26,620
I got one! Up you go!

372
00:19:27,280 --> 00:19:29,200
Heck yeah, I got a shiwami!

373
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:32,980
I'm not gonna let you beat me! I-I win!

374
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:36,477
I'll let Hulemy take the prize,
but second place is mine!

375
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,390
Gotcha!

376
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:39,720
It'll break!

377
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:41,960
Grab the line, not the rod! Okay!

378
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,717
You hooked a fish monster! Reel it in!

379
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,800
I hear those things are delicious.

380
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,380
Look what I caught!

381
00:19:54,220 --> 00:19:56,320
So she really caught a monster?

382
00:19:57,560 --> 00:19:58,390
Huh?

383
00:19:58,980 --> 00:20:01,280
Wait, did my hook snag on something?

384
00:20:02,680 --> 00:20:06,577
The line might break if I pull any
harder, but this could be the big one.

385
00:20:06,660 --> 00:20:07,880
I'm gonna go for it.

386
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:11,780
Oh, did you get a bite too, Boxo?

387
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:13,400
Hello there.

388
00:20:13,780 --> 00:20:14,662
Need some help?

389
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:15,960
Yes, please.

390
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:17,475
I've got you covered.

391
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:22,780
That is one enormous clam.

392
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:25,537
I've never seen a monster
that looks like that.

393
00:20:25,620 --> 00:20:26,914
Maybe it's a mutation?

394
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:28,257
You think it's tasty?

395
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:29,458
There's no telling.

396
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:31,856
But I'm curious, so let's cook it up.

397
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:35,420
This beast is looking good.

398
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:38,277
Master Boxo, I've been
searching high and low.

399
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:39,977
What are you doing out here?

400
00:20:40,060 --> 00:20:41,472
Wow, that's a nice fish.

401
00:20:41,660 --> 00:20:43,320
Oh, is that thing a clam?

402
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:46,020
Big clam.

403
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:48,520
It even took me shwell by surprise.

404
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:51,984
Huh, now I'm extra curious
to see what's inside.

405
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:54,860
Way too good.

406
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,517
You should have some too, Mishuel.

407
00:20:56,600 --> 00:20:57,718
Don't mind if I do.

408
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:01,018
If Shui were here, she'd
probably eat it all herself.

409
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:02,520
Is that a challenge?

410
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:10,337
I'm going to need you to wipe
that greedy look off your face.

411
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:11,361
Everyone's here.

412
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:14,200
Now we can get the
seaside barbecue started.

413
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:18,020
Is that... No way. What the?

414
00:21:18,520 --> 00:21:21,579
They're both looking at
that clam like they know it.

415
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:24,840
Shui, do you recognize that creature?

416
00:21:26,040 --> 00:21:28,040
Sure do, I thought the same thing.

417
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:29,520
What else could it be?

418
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:44,860
Wait, what?

419
00:21:45,100 --> 00:21:46,217
Is that some kind of monster?

420
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:48,600
Uh, so what was that about?

421
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:49,959
I beg your pardon.

422
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:52,041
That clam looked rather familiar.

423
00:21:57,240 --> 00:21:59,420
It's so hot. Yikes.

424
00:21:59,760 --> 00:22:02,337
That's not how you should
be treating poor pity.

425
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:03,640
A harmless shut-in.

426
00:22:35,180 --> 00:22:38,480
I don't know.

427
00:23:01,120 --> 00:23:02,677
Thank you

428
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:09,760
so

429
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:17,339
much for watching.

430
00:23:35,760 --> 00:23:37,980
I look forward to serving you again.
